            {
                "entry_id": "bac95f26-ef92-36a6-b987-b9e24d3decec",
                "word": "trawieniec",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07c736f6-412b-3339-a3fa-20297a12167f",
                        "entry_id": "bac95f26-ef92-36a6-b987-b9e24d3decec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "gruczołowa część żołądka przeżuwaczy, o gruszkowatym kształcie, tworząca czwarty przedział"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d28df89a-f4ce-4647-a578-4e9aabbb1c85",
                                "sense_id": "07c736f6-412b-3339-a3fa-20297a12167f",
                                "text": "Główną funkcją trawieńca jest trawienie białek."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "38bfcac9-d300-4da4-8c2c-26f1f1c825ec",
                        "source_entry_id": "bac95f26-ef92-36a6-b987-b9e24d3decec",
                        "source_sense_id": "07c736f6-412b-3339-a3fa-20297a12167f",
                        "target_lang_word": "abomasum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "abomasum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e0796cd7-c1b5-392a-b0f2-915aa94455d6",
                                        "entry_id": "abf5e067-9b78-3530-992f-feaa3944dae8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The fourth digestive compartment of the stomach of a cow or other ruminant, after the omasum;"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "283b9263-db9a-48a9-bcb0-3426f8372137",
                                                "sense_id": "e0796cd7-c1b5-392a-b0f2-915aa94455d6",
                                                "text": "The abomasa of sheep grazing on natural pastures in the highveld of Zimbabwe were examined at Mt. Hampden abattoir between October 1985 and September 1986 for H. contortus. Of 304 abomasa, 213 (70%) harboured H. contortus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "253915ec-32c2-4b1d-9136-be7f7973ad40",
                                                "sense_id": "e0796cd7-c1b5-392a-b0f2-915aa94455d6",
                                                "text": "1996 [1991, Ellis Horwood Limited], R. K. Robinson, A. Y. Tamime, Feta & Related Cheeses, Woodhead Publishing Limited, page 54,\nTraditionally, coagulation of the milk for Feta cheese manufacture was achieved using rennet produced by cheesemakers themselves from the abomasa of lambs and kids slaughtered before weaning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d85a61af-9bad-4e42-8234-3aee35221c30",
                                                "sense_id": "e0796cd7-c1b5-392a-b0f2-915aa94455d6",
                                                "text": "Digesta, which are compressed inside the omasal body, are forced onwards into the abomasum by a gradually increasing and prolonged contraction of the omasal body (which starts after the first or second contraction of the omasal canal)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab0e46ce-a8ae-4dff-8323-42bdd875144b",
                                                "sense_id": "e0796cd7-c1b5-392a-b0f2-915aa94455d6",
                                                "text": "In the newborn ruminant the abomasum is about as large as the rumen and remains relatively large as long as only milk is consumed (Brugnone, 1809)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed0b54f2-ecec-3acb-a0e9-d338824124ff",
                                        "entry_id": "abf5e067-9b78-3530-992f-feaa3944dae8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The fourth digestive compartment of the stomach of a cow or other ruminant, after the omasum;\\nthe lining of said compartment, considered as a foodstuff.",
                                            "the lining of said compartment, considered as a foodstuff."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d81f17e-fea1-4653-bdc2-3ff7394c74f0",
                        "source_entry_id": "bac95f26-ef92-36a6-b987-b9e24d3decec",
                        "source_sense_id": "07c736f6-412b-3339-a3fa-20297a12167f",
                        "target_lang_word": "maw",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "maw",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a3ee87e-e666-3267-90fe-7a97c5dd8a6f",
                                        "entry_id": "6e0c197b-0993-3568-bd44-3df730903f2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The stomach, especially of an animal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a82bd43-4595-4b4e-8642-01cc39af8ca4",
                                                "sense_id": "8a3ee87e-e666-3267-90fe-7a97c5dd8a6f",
                                                "text": "So Death shall be deceav'd his glut, and with us two / Be forc'd to satisfie his Rav'nous Maw."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "834faf36-d7aa-3df9-855f-bea08dd274ff",
                                        "entry_id": "6e0c197b-0993-3568-bd44-3df730903f2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The upper digestive tract (where food enters the body), especially the mouth and jaws of a fearsome and ravenous creature; craw."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6298bcd2-4dab-437e-812f-7e851cf9ff96",
                                                "sense_id": "834faf36-d7aa-3df9-855f-bea08dd274ff",
                                                "text": "To save poor lambkins from the eagle's maw"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af66f0dd-85ca-4d38-a2e7-c54003ee0f57",
                                                "sense_id": "834faf36-d7aa-3df9-855f-bea08dd274ff",
                                                "text": "“I saw the opening maw of hell, With endless pains and sorrows there; Which none but they that feel can tell— Oh, I was plunging to despair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bbf28b54-b4de-3fce-88dc-30d327f387df",
                                        "entry_id": "6e0c197b-0993-3568-bd44-3df730903f2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The mouth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1575d065-ae45-40c9-9998-f5d80d6e031a",
                                                "sense_id": "bbf28b54-b4de-3fce-88dc-30d327f387df",
                                                "text": "Shut your maw!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61b1d4df-9588-4305-a758-d2a26b4762fa",
                                                "sense_id": "bbf28b54-b4de-3fce-88dc-30d327f387df",
                                                "text": "She fumbled with her bag, and produced from its little maw a scented handkerchief."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f8fa305-7afd-3641-8c07-a674f9cfe56a",
                                        "entry_id": "6e0c197b-0993-3568-bd44-3df730903f2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any large, insatiable or perilous opening."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e09789cc-7a6b-4290-98c0-f27c450ce01e",
                                                "sense_id": "9f8fa305-7afd-3641-8c07-a674f9cfe56a",
                                                "text": "Adam requires a touch of feminine lace and a whisper of diaphanous silk, not a direct vision of the gaping maw of the human vulva."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "386dd346-4073-4fa2-9896-71f23bfdc8fe",
                                                "sense_id": "9f8fa305-7afd-3641-8c07-a674f9cfe56a",
                                                "text": "One two! I was born in a cross-fire hurricane. And I howled at the maw in the drivin' rain. But it's all right now, in fact, it's a gas. But it's all right. I'm Jumpin' Jack Flash. It's a gas, gas, gas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11c99ad9-af44-31e2-a8a1-208f35b9beb3",
                                        "entry_id": "6e0c197b-0993-3568-bd44-3df730903f2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Appetite; inclination."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "202380c2-ac19-4958-b034-2f6276a18c27",
                                                "sense_id": "11c99ad9-af44-31e2-a8a1-208f35b9beb3",
                                                "text": "Unless you had more maw to do me good."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e8e3aa8-f6c4-3b7d-8847-216cbed5fc68",
                                        "entry_id": "6e0c197b-0993-3568-bd44-3df730903f2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The swim bladder of a fish, especially when used as food in Chinese cuisine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c8e60c1-8957-403a-a15e-53b2131696c3",
                                                "sense_id": "0e8e3aa8-f6c4-3b7d-8847-216cbed5fc68",
                                                "text": "fish maw: The buoyancy bladder of a fish similar in appearance to the mammalian lung. The maw of the conger pike is used in Chinese cooking and is usually sold in dried form which needs reconstituting for about 3 hours and treating with[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d3e5753-0434-42db-ab2b-d3a1b013836f",
                                                "sense_id": "0e8e3aa8-f6c4-3b7d-8847-216cbed5fc68",
                                                "text": "Fish maw is the commercial term for the dried swim bladders of large fish like sturgeon. Fish maw has no fishy taste and absorbs the flavors of other ingredients."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c9eeb5a-5b1e-4e5c-af0e-05b6e144a834",
                                                "sense_id": "0e8e3aa8-f6c4-3b7d-8847-216cbed5fc68",
                                                "text": "Fish maw (swim bladder) is easily obtainable from your local fishmonger[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5e17bac-3575-4c50-a1bd-4dc16bb1d5ce",
                                                "sense_id": "0e8e3aa8-f6c4-3b7d-8847-216cbed5fc68",
                                                "text": "[...] fish maw is light, white in color, and has a spongy texture. Dried fish maw is tasteless which makes it a good complementary addition to many dishes since it can absorb the flavors of other ingredients when it is cooked with other food[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
